---
layout: base.njk
workspace: true
scripts: ["/js/file-options.js", "/js/tool-ui.js", "/js/image.js"]
---
{# image.njk — Layout for pages with the image compressor. Pages supply their words in the front matter.
  Facts and questions shared by every image page live here and in src/_data/imageFaq.json. #}
<h1>{{ h1 }}</h1>
<p class="s">{{ intro | safe }}</p>
{%- if limit %}
<div class="limit"><b>{{ limit.big }}</b><span>{{ limit.caption }}</span></div>
{%- endif %}
{% include "partials/imagetool.njk" %}
<details class="supporting"><summary>Help, size guides and questions</summary>
<div class="supporting-content">
<p class="also">Need to shrink a video instead? <a href="/">Compress a video&nbsp;→</a></p>
{%- set sizes = imageSizes %}
{% include "partials/sizelinks.njk" %}
{{ content | safe }}
<h2>What to know</h2>
<ul>
  {%- for f in facts %}
  <li>{{ f | safe }}</li>
  {%- endfor %}
  <li>The result is a JPG, which almost every form and website accepts. Transparent areas become white.</li>
  <li>It lowers the JPG quality first, and only makes the image smaller in pixels if that is not enough.</li>
  <li>It counts 1KB as 1000 bytes, so the result fits whichever way a site measures KB.</li>
  <li>Location and camera details saved in the photo are left out of the result.</li>
  <li>If a form asks for exact pixel dimensions, open “Set pixel dimensions” above. A tighter KB limit may not fit at those dimensions.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
  {%- for item in imageFaq %}
  <details><summary>{{ item.q }}</summary><p>{{ item.a }}</p></details>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>
</div></details>
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ { page: page, site: site, h1: h1, description: description, faq: imageFaq } | toolSchema | safe }}</script>
